; Railway's Nixpacks build always runs `npm ci` during its install phase regardless of any
; custom buildCommand — a plain custom command in railway.json/dashboard settings gets appended
; as a separate step, it doesn't replace the auto-detected install. This file is the one thing
; npm itself always honors no matter which command invokes it, so it's what actually stops
; node-gyp from trying to rebuild better-sqlite3 (the container has no Python, so that rebuild
; always fails) — same reasoning as the --ignore-scripts flag documented in the root README for
; local dev, just applied at a layer Railway can't route around.
ignore-scripts=true
